* t33ctrl.a -- CONF68K test t33: the negative control for the locking group.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): an access that no other path has locked succeeds* immediately. That sounds like nothing, and it is the most important test in* this group.** Every other two-process test here concludes "the lock held" from a non-zero* observation -- 252 for a refusal, 901 for an access that only got through* once the holder let go. All of them would still report exactly that if the* fork/rescue harness itself were broken so as to never return 0: a contend* that always timed out, a child that always died, a marker protocol that* always looked blocked. Nothing in the group could tell the difference* between "locking works" and "this harness cannot say otherwise".** This test is the other half. The parent deliberately holds NOTHING: it* builds the file, closes the path it created it on -- the create is what* takes the EOF lock, and the close is what drops it -- and reopens READ-only,* which cannot auto-lock, then never reads. The child's write must therefore* come straight back, and contend must report 0.** Because the parent holds no lock, the answer does not depend on the device* having record locking at all: 0 on an RBF image, 0 on a host-native* directory. So this one does NOT probe with canlock and does NOT skip -- it* is the only two-process test that runs everywhere, which also makes it the* only one CI ever exercises. A change that breaks fork.i now fails a test* on every push instead of only in the local --rbf gate.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1IOpen set $84ICreate set $83IWrite set $8AISeek set $88IClose set $8FIDelete set $87ATTRS set $001BUPDATE set 3RDONLY set 1*EXPECT set 0* psect t33ctrl,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,4096,startstart bsr ckrole tst.w d0 bne.w child** ---- parent: build the file, then hold nothing at all ---- lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #3,d0 trap #0 dc.w IDelete lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #2,d0 move.w #ATTRS,d1 clr.l d2 trap #0 dc.w ICreate bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d7 lea data50(pc),a0 moveq #50,d1 moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IWrite bcs.w setuperr lea data50(pc),a0 moveq #50,d1 moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IWrite bcs.w setuperr* Closing the creating path is what makes this a control: a file's creator* holds the EOF lock from the moment it is created, and only the close lets* it go. moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IClose** Read mode, not update: a path that cannot modify what it reads never* acquires a record lock. And it never reads, so it cannot pick up the end* of the file either. lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #RDONLY,d0 trap #0 dc.w IOpen bcs.w setuperr move.w d0,d7* bsr contend bcs.w setuperr* moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IClose cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail** ---- child: write where nobody is holding anything ----child lea fname(pc),a0 moveq #UPDATE,d0 trap #0 dc.w IOpen bcs.w chfail move.w d0,d7* No chticks here, deliberately. SS_Ticks bounds a wait, and this child has* nothing to wait for -- the parent holds no lock. Asking for it would make* the test device-dependent again: a host-native path has no record locking,* so SS_Ticks answers E$UnkSvc there, and the child would report ERROR 208 on* the one medium this test exists to run on. Measured, not predicted. clr.l d1 moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w ISeek bcs.w chfail bsr chready lea data50(pc),a0 moveq #10,d1 moveq #0,d0 move.w d7,d0 trap #0 dc.w IWrite bcc.s chok moveq #0,d6 move.w d1,d6 bra.s chrepchok moveq #0,d6chrep bsr chsaw bra.w chdone* use verdict.i use fork.i use report.i*fname dc.b "SCRATCH/t33.dat",0myname dc.b "t33ctrl",0data50 dc.b "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678" dc.b 13idstr dc.b "RESULT t33 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0skipstr dc.b "SKIP",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  an access nobody has locked comes straight back",0 ends